From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mali_kbase: force non-ACK VMA gap-search path in mali_kbase_mmap.c

The build was failing at the final modpost/link stage with:
  ERROR: modpost: "vm_unmapped_area" [midgard/mali_kbase.ko] undefined!

Root cause is NOT a missing kernel export to add. gpu.mk (line 29:
GPU_KERNEL_CFLAGS = KCFLAGS="${KCFLAGS} -D__ANDROID_COMMON_KERNEL__")
unconditionally defines __ANDROID_COMMON_KERNEL__ for every CIX
product build -- it is literally Cix's Android-product Makefile
("Description: build GPU kernel module for cix Android product"),
reused verbatim for this non-Android NCZ desktop-Linux target without
stripping the Android-only flag.

That macro makes kbase_unmapped_area_topdown() (this file, previously
line 274) take the branch that calls the core kernel's
vm_unmapped_area() directly. That call is only safe on the Android
Common Kernel, where Google carries a vendor patch that
EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL()s it. Mainline Linux has never exported this
symbol: confirmed by direct inspection of every stable tag from v6.6
through the current v6.19 development tree in this kernel's own git
history (mm/mmap.c has zero EXPORT_SYMBOL* for vm_unmapped_area in any
of them, while sibling functions in the same file -- mm_get_unmapped_area,
find_vma_intersection, find_vma, vm_munmap -- are all exported). This
is not an oversight: a 2016 upstream RFC asking for exactly this
export for exactly this reason ("mm: Export symbols unmapped_area() &
unmapped_area_topdown()", GPU/SVM driver justification, Olujide
Ogunbowale, reviewed by Christoph Hellwig) was never merged and the
symbol remains unexported a decade later. Patching this kernel to add
EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(vm_unmapped_area) would mean carrying, indefinitely,
a kernel-internal-API export that upstream has specifically declined,
for a driver that -- per the next paragraph -- does not actually need
it.

kbase_unmapped_area_topdown() already ships a complete, self-contained
non-ACK implementation for kernel >= 6.1 (the
"#else /* __ANDROID_COMMON_KERNEL__ */" branch, previously line 347)
built entirely on MA_STATE/mas_empty_area_rev() -- direct maple-tree
primitives already EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL'd in this kernel's own
lib/maple_tree.c (confirmed) -- with zero dependency on
vm_unmapped_area(). This is kbase upstream's own intended code path
for non-Android kernels; we are simply not currently reaching it
because of the misapplied Android build flag.

The align_and_check() helper that path calls is gated by the sibling
guard "#if (KERNEL_VERSION(6, 1, 0) > LINUX_VERSION_CODE) ||
!defined(__ANDROID_COMMON_KERNEL__)" a few lines above (previously
line 105), so both guards must flip together for this kernel version
(7.2.0, >= 6.1.0) to compile: this patch's single #undef, placed after
the version_compat_defs.h include has already resolved its own
ACK-conditional inline helpers against the real, unmodified build
flag, flips both consistently for this translation unit only.

Deliberately scoped to this file alone (not a recipe-wide
GPU_KERNEL_CFLAGS override) so every other driver file keeps
__ANDROID_COMMON_KERNEL__ defined and its behavior byte-for-byte
unchanged -- notably mali_kbase_mem_migrate.c's
kbase_page_migration_enabled default (0 vs -1), which was already
carried through the page-migration API port in a prior patch set and
should not be silently re-toggled by this fix. (The other
__ANDROID_COMMON_KERNEL__ sites in include/linux/version_compat_defs.h
are kernel-version-gated against thresholds all below 7.2.0 and are
confirmed dead/identical either way at this kernel version, so this
file-local #undef changes nothing there even though that header is
shared.)

No kernel source is touched by this fix.

Codex (gpt-5.5) adversarial-reviewed this patch read-only against the
live driver + kernel trees before it was applied: APPROVE, with the
caveat that the maple-tree branch's fidelity to kbase's shader-code
and 4GB-boundary constraints (not the ACK path's start_gap handling,
which this driver never used anyway) should be confirmed by a
functional GPU test after deploy, not compile success alone.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/thirdparty/mali_kbase_mmap.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/thirdparty/mali_kbase_mmap.c
@@ -14,6 +14,13 @@
 #include <mali_kbase.h>
 #include <mali_kbase_reg_track.h>
 
+/* CIX NCZ (non-Android target): force the maple-tree-based (non-ACK)
+ * top-down VMA gap search in this file only -- see commit message for
+ * why __ANDROID_COMMON_KERNEL__ must stay defined everywhere else in
+ * the driver.
+ */
+#undef __ANDROID_COMMON_KERNEL__
+
 /* mali_kbase_mmap.c
  *
  * This file contains Linux specific implementation of
